test/check/error-constants.sumspec:18:17:
   |
18 | Decimal = Count(1.5)
   |                 ^
Count is an __int, so 1.5 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:19:16:
   |
19 | Text = Percent("a")
   |                ^
Percent is a __float, so "a" doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:20:15:
   |
20 | Number = Name(3)
   |               ^
Name is a __text, so 3 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:21:14:
   |
21 | Opaque = Tag(1)
   |              ^
Tag is an atomic with no base, so 1 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:22:12:
   |
22 | Enum = Gps(1)
   |            ^
Gps is an enumeration, so 1 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:23:11:
   |
23 | Unknown = Missing(1)
   |           ^
unknown type Missing; declare it in __atomics or define it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:24:15:
   |
24 | Product = Box(1)
   |               ^
Box is neither a number, text nor an enumeration, so 1 doesn't fit it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:25:18:
   |
25 | BadVariant = Gps.Missing
   |                  ^
Missing is not a variant of Gps

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:26:24:
   |
26 | PayloadVariant = Shape.Circle
   |                        ^
Shape.Circle has a payload, so it can't be written as a value; test it with a pattern

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:27:11:
   |
27 | NotASum = Count.Zero
   |           ^
a constant variant is written Type.Variant, where Type is a sum; Count is not

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:28:14:
   |
28 | UnknownSum = Missing.Zero
   |              ^
unknown type Missing; declare it in __atomics or define it

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:30:1:
   |
30 | Twice = Count(2)
   | ^
Twice is defined twice (first on line 29)

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:31:1:
   |
31 | Gps = Count(3)
   | ^
Gps is defined as a type and as a constant

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:32:1:
   |
32 | Taken = Count(4)
   | ^
Taken is declared in __atomics and also defined as a constant

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:34:9:
   |
34 | Alias = Cycle
   |         ^
Cycle is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:37:11:
   |
37 | Wrapped = Fine
   |           ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:38:20:
   |
38 | Factor = Percent * Fine
   |                    ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:39:16:
   |
39 | Payload = Wrap Fine | Other
   |                ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:40:19:
   |
40 | Boxed = Percent * Cycle
   |                   ^
Cycle is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:42:7:
   |
42 | go :: Fine -> Fine
   |       ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:42:15:
   |
42 | go :: Fine -> Fine
   |               ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:45:11:
   |
45 | Listed = [Fine]
   |           ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:46:19:
   |
46 | Keyed = [Count by Fine]
   |                   ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:48:7:
   |
48 | input Fine :: Count -> Count'
   |       ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:49:12:
   |
49 | arg :: App(Fine) -> App(Count')
   |            ^
Fine is a constant, not a type; it can only be compared in a guard

test/check/error-constants.sumspec:50:34:
   |
50 | dotted :: App => Count#k // k == Fine.Foo -> Count'
   |                                  ^
Fine is a constant, so it has no variants

